  "purpose": "Post-implementation replay of the declared bounded lifecycle; not a proof of the Rust implementation",
  "assumptions": [
    "enabled_transitions is a caller-declared relation over a six-step trace",
    "Cold/read permits one initialization; FullScan means an ordinary subsequent read scanned the whole graph",
    "Current/read must reuse storage; Dirty/read must apply only affected records",
    "SQLite trigger completeness, query plans, scope isolation and concurrency are checked by code review and Rust tests, not this model",
    "Schema/database replacement recovery is outside this ordinary-operation trace",
    "Solver responses report cached=true because the exact declared facts match the earlier replay"
